Z||000000||Richard Parnell||07-06-2001||02:25 PM||||As you know I used your kit in doing the v8 conversion on my '87 coupe.  The only real problem I have is the passenger side deck hinge.  We cut it some to clear the inside valve cover.  The only problem is that I cannot remove the valve cover to adjust the valves.  I would like to cut the hinge a little more but the bolt looks to be in the way.  Can I eliminate the lower bolt and still have enough strength left in the hinge.  I really would like to be able to remove the valve cover without dropping the cradle.  Any advice would be appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Archie||07-06-2001||03:04 PM||||Cut the hinge box right at the bottom of that stud sticking out.<P>Then what I do is to remove the stud that is sticking out and replace it with a bolt & nut. Then remove the bolt & nut to make clearance.||||reg||1
